# Week-03 Status — Data Memory (RAM) Integration

## Summary

Implemented direct-addressing instructions `MOV A,addr` and `MOV addr,A` to enable programs to read from and write to the 256-byte Data Memory (RAM).

## Memory Design

The MS51FB9AE simulator has two memory areas, both implemented as `int[]` (unsigned 8-bit values stored in Java ints):

| Area            | Purpose              | Size    | Access          |
| --------------- | -------------------- | ------- | --------------- |
| Program Memory  | Instruction storage   | 16 KB   | Read-only (ROM) |
| Data Memory     | Runtime data storage  | 256 B   | Read/Write (RAM)|

- **`readData(addr)`** returns the byte at RAM[addr]
- **`writeData(addr, value)`** stores `value & 0xFF` at RAM[addr]
- **`clearDataMemory()`** zeros all 256 bytes (used by CPU `reset()`)
- Address validation throws `IllegalArgumentException` for addresses outside 0–255

## New Instructions

| Mnemonic      | Opcode | Bytes | Operation               |
| ------------- | ------ | ----- | ----------------------- |
| `MOV A,addr`  | 0xE5   | 2     | A ← RAM[addr]           |
| `MOV addr,A`  | 0xF5   | 2     | RAM[addr] ← A           |

These match the real 8051 instruction set direct-addressing opcodes.

